{%- comment -%}
  Site fonts, rendered in <head>.

  Kontrapunkt display face (Bold 700, Light 300).
  Kontrapunkt by Kontrapunkt A/S, CC BY-SA 3.0 (kontrapunkt.com/type).
  The woff2 files are straight format conversions of the original OTFs,
  with the glyphs unchanged.
  Use var(--font-display) for key display type: the footer wordmark, header
  menu, section headings and piece titles. Labels stay on the mono stack.

  Unsteady Oversteer by Ray Larabie (CC0, public domain): the punch face,
  var(--font-punch), used only for the footer wordmark. Always set it in
  uppercase: its uppercase is a squared unicase, and its lowercase glyphs
  are inverted white-on-black blocks.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'kontrapunkt-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Kontrapunkt';
    src: url('{{ 'kontrapunkt-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Kontrapunkt';
    src: url('{{ 'kontrapunkt-light.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Unsteady Oversteer';
    src: url('{{ 'unsteady-oversteer.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  :root {
    --font-punch: 'Unsteady Oversteer', var(--font-display, sans-serif);
    --font-display: 'Kontrapunkt', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: ui-monospace, 'SFMono-Regular', Menlo, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', monospace;
  }
</style>
